				<r3d:description language="eng">ORA (Oxford University Research Archive) is the institutional repository for the University of Oxford. ORA was established in 2007 as a permanent and secure online archive of research materials produced by members of the University of Oxford.
ORA aims to provide access to the full text of as much of Oxford&#039;s academic research as possible. This includes articles, conference papers, theses, research data, working papers, posters and more.
Making materials open access removes barriers that restrict access to research, allowing for free dissemination of full text content, available to anyone with Internet access. ORA promotes and encourages the sharing of the scholarly output produced by the members of the University of Oxford that have been published under open access conditions, whilst additionally supporting University compliance with research funder policy and assessment.</r3d:description>
